pre-push guards the public Apache-2.0 repo (origin, github.com/hanzoai/cloud).
It refuses a push to origin when either is true:
  HISTORY  a pushed commit is reachable from a private remote's ref. Private
           means every refs/remotes/ namespace except origin -- forge, gh,
           inc, inc2 and stale leftovers. Refs you never fetched are not
           consulted, so a fresh clone still pushes.
  IMPORTS  a pushed .go or go.mod blob references github.com/hanzo-inc/...,
           hanzoai/authz, hanzoai/licensing or hanzoai/metrics. It reads the
           commits' trees, not your working tree. luxfi/kms is public.
Other remotes and branch deletions are not checked.  Install:  git config core.hooksPath .githooks
